Dynamics implied by [[REF:prop:delay]] and [[REF:cor:period]]. Panel (a): impulse responses of $u_{t+1}=u_t-g\,u_{t-k}$ at ninety per cent of the critical gain, for $k=1$, $2$ and $4$, each normalised to unit maximum. Convergence is oscillatory and the period is $4k+2$ quarters, as the corollary states. Panel (b): the spectral radius crosses one exactly at $g=g^\star(k)$ for every $k$, and the slope of the crossing falls as $k$ rises. This is the reason a near-threshold instability at a long lag needs hundreds of quarters to become visible in amplitude, and hence the reason [[REF:sec:power]] rests the inference on the autocorrelation function rather than on the amplitude.
